# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  THE DATABASE PROOFS CI RUNS — and the ones it cannot, with the reason.
#
#  Every tests/proofs/*.db.js file appears here exactly once
#  (tests/gates/gate_db_proof_manifest.js refuses an unlisted proof).
#
#    run      <file>            CI runs it against a schema built from the
#                               migration chain and FAILS the job if it fails.
#    backlog  <file>  <reason>  CI still runs it and REPORTS it, but a failure
#                               does not fail the job. The reason is the
#                               condition that moves it to `run`. A backlog
#                               proof that passes is flagged: promote it.
#
#  A green job means "every `run` proof passed", nothing more. The backlog
#  is visible debt, not hidden debt. First classification 2026-09-04 from
#  a full sweep against a fresh chain-built database (CURRENT_STATE #17).
# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
